; DECISIONS — present-truth ledger
    One entry per decision: what holds, why (short), decided-by, date, cite.
    Append or expressly overturn; never silently rewrite. Lower entries supersede earlier ones. History and deliberation live in CHANGELOG.md and the cited records -- this file stays thin.

    Cite decisions by slugged link, never bare ordinal: identifiers that will be *read* carry their referent's name (e.g. [[DECISIONS#d1-some-slug|D1 some-slug]]).

    decided-by vocabulary:
      steward    - steward made the call; agent or council ratified
      ratified   - agent made the call; steward ratified
      council    - agent call after red-teaming + unified validation from other agents
      supported  - agent call with provisional steward/council support; easier revisit
      defacto    - "decided" without really being decided; recorded so the record exists
      proposed   - from steward or any agent; not blocking anything yet
      transition - rejected but still existing somewhere; defacto-but-being-fixed

; Deploy-time seed -- fill the [placeholders], then uncomment by deleting this comment line and outdenting the block:
  |decision[decided-by-vocabulary]
    :holds The seven-value decided-by vocabulary above governs this ledger.
    :why The weight of a decision is who stood behind it and how.
    :decided-by [steward-or-ratified]
    :date <[deploy-date]>
    :cite [your-project] deployment of the verisectorium template.
